{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood","id":1558625,"title":"Kindred venues that sell blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-03T17:09:35-08:00","id":1558625,"title":"Kindred venues that sell blood","content":"Something I've seen in various chronicles is a place where Kindred cannot only relax or party (like the Succubus Club), but also provides vitae to Kindred. By that, I mean blood is a commodity provided to them for sale at such places, they are not simply a location where Kindred can hunt or bring their own herd to feed on. The owner of the premises offers blood as a menu item. It's something I remember seeing a lot in chronicles both tabletop and LARP. (In the Succubus Club itself, I think the intention was simply to allow Kindred to hunt there at a much lower Difficulty.)<br /> <br /> On a certain level this makes sense. One would want &quot;refreshment&quot; when one relaxes or parties. However, the logistics of this for Kindred are much harder than for mortals. Even if we assume this is just extra Herd being available (as opposed to cold blood), it has to be a pain in the ass to make available enough blood. Living people used as Herd are much more likely to be killed during feeding by customers than they would by the Herd's owner. Making cold blood available in mass quantities is a risk to the Masquerade. Running out of blood might risk Kindred going into frenzy as they get angry about being denied &quot;service&quot;.<br /> <br /> So is this actually a plausible scenario? Or is it just not worth the hassle?<br /> <br /> If you think it is plausible, what should the cost of that be? I don't remember payment being an issue as usually it was just handwaved by the STs.<br /> <br /> If you put it purely in financial terms, Kindred with high Resources might want to simply buy whatever they need and avoid the hassle of hunting. If you make payment be in something else, what makes sense? I don't think boons would work well for various reasons. Kindred are unlikely want to be into prestation debt for something so trivial, or if you make it too cheap, the proprietor is unlikely to make use of so many trivial boons (or simply managing to accurately record it all). Is there something else that could be easily used as &quot;currency&quot; that would be both convenient and still valuable?<br /> <br /> Instead of actual financial transaction, does anyone suggest an alternate way of handling this (other than making it a rare exception for especially trusted friends of the proprietor) where vitae is &quot;for sale&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T23:37:22-08:00","id":1558631,"title":"","content":"I'm not really familiar with V5 but at least in the older source books, I don't think that there are any places where you con just buy blood.<br /> <br /> I also don't think that buying or selling bag blood has ever been covered in these editions. Personally I would probably handwave it as a version of the Herd background, and sellling blood (be it warm or cold) basically as renting out your herd.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the finacial terms I think the important part is to to set the cost in a way that it keeps the herd and the resources background balanced, meaning you shouldn't make more money by renintig out your herd, that a resource background would give you, and get more blood from resources than you would get from the herd background of equal value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T00:05:26-08:00","id":1558632,"title":"","content":"Daybreakers (2009) had that not so original idea of industrial &quot;blood farms&quot;. Sure, in that scenario the vampires have become the dominant species and Humans became an endangered species but the basic idea is actually very plausible -just in the USA about 600,000 - 650,000 people go missing in the United States <i>annually </i>and this isthe reports that are <i>filed</i>. Most cases are resolved quickly, but about 1% of cases remain open long-term, but as of early 2025, over 25,500 cases remained open in the NamUs database.<br /> This is just playing with numbers and plenty room to wiggle around, because this data based on who been actually reported and papers filled - but sadly way more people fly under the radar and disapear without a trace or notice, homeless people for example and other unfortunate souls who ended up on the bottom of the barrel.<br /> So a Vampire scooping up, lets say 100 Human, keep them in an underground lab/werehouse in a vegetative/lobotomized state, wired to a machine to keep them alive just to harves their blood?<br /> Not even that impossible nor a logistical nightmare<br /> <br /> Another good business to set up a nice Blood donation fraud - just in reverse - it is - again, sadly - a common scam where individuals, posing as genuine donors, take advantage of patients' or their families' desperation during a medical emergency by demanding upfront payment for travel expenses and then disappearing.<br /> As the Analyst said in Matrix: Humans; you people believe the <i>craziest shit</i> .<br /> It is actually true<br /> And taking advantage of good nature is easy<br /> Forging documents, seting up a whole faux Blood donor-drive, tracking shipments, with a TechWiz Nosferatu on your side it is easy to make an untracable (of course nothing is foolproof, and that could be the good source of story, find the leak for example) hussle, where a bunch of your &quot;Doctors and nurses&quot; travel around in a blood drive, smiling and taking blood from the happy donors. Blood that only lands in hopsitals on paper.. but those hospitals may not even exist. Just on papers. Etc.<br /> <br /> Having a huge herd you provide for others is another good option, making hunting super-easy or if they relegious sect or cult, blood sacrifice is part of the faith and pratices and after the sermon you ends up with gallons of blood; not necesarily human sacrifice (but again, could be done that too) juts standing around of the altar, cut your palm and offer your blood to [insert whatever you want here] - and the cravings of the Altar not only draws a nice sigil (visuals are always important; that good old pazazz!) but leand the blood down to gather in jugs<br /> Or unfer the chamber another chamber where blood literally rains on the vampires to have a literal blood orgy...<br /> <br /> V20 introduced the Kisayd mixologists and bartenders who provide blood mixture refreshments ranging from human ('ol chap, I've heard 83' blond virgin in an iced glass with just a hint of a &quot;spicy&quot; blood of a brutish brawler is expecialyl tasty!) to exotic like Garou or Fea blood for the kick - and they works in Elysiums!<br /> But even berofre that the Followers of Set who praticed Akhu had the basic rite called &quot;Milk of Set&quot; that brewed fremented Blood beer that actually could make a Kindred drunk and they sold it gleefully to anyone who wanted to serve some extra - including in Elysiums<br /> Even before that there was a bit forgotten secondary skill from &quot;Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand&quot;.on page 70, named &quot;Blood Preparation&quot;: - You are knowledgeable in chemicals, intoxicants, herbs, spices and food and how they affect mortal and inmortal blood. You can prepare a variety of flavours for blood feasts<br /> Blood foods, blood-bread, blood-puding, blood-wine, several blood sweets... a nice feast is always fun in an Elysium or in an Elder's banquet hall especially if your host is on the Via Voluptarius/Path of Pleasure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Vampire parties can be fun<br /> <br /> The price is easy really, a Vampire Bar could sell these things for money - figuring out is just economy how much you have to spend versus how much you have to ask to break even (you not necesarily have to make profit, the existance of such establishment itself is huge<br /> And lazy vampires? &quot;Food delivery service&quot; is nothing more than providing the right meal masked as an escort service using your herd; in this case your herd is carefulyl crafted to satisfy the needs of others not yours - from the virgin welsh midget sumo wrestlers to the elderly and anything including but not limited to the not-that legal to meet the pickiest Ventrue's needs<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> Boons and Favors of course is the bread and butter and foundation of the Cainite community but money is money<br /> It is more about Fame and Trust<br /> Batman villains buy their secret hideouts from the same person, known as <b>The Broker</b>.<br /> Originally a normal real estate agent in Gotham City, he realized that the constant destruction of property by supervillains could be profitable so he specializes in finding abandoned factories, closed zoos, old shelters, and forgotten warehouses, matching them to the specific, often eccentric, needs of criminals.<br /> He has provided lairs to major villains, including the Joker, Penguin, and Mr. Freeze.<br /> The Broker operates on a high-turnover model where he sells a hideout, Batman destroys it, and the villain returns to buy a new one, creating a consistent business cycle.<br /> He operates on a strict &quot;cash only, no real names&quot; policy and hires snipers for protection during meetings to ensure his safety in the criminal underworld.<br /> And while Batman is well aware his business only tried I think once to ask him where Victor Zsasz's new base of operation is; I think some kids went missing? And the guy had the balls of steel and kept his mouth shut. And while had to drown his conscience sometimes in whisky, he is still alive and reap a nice profit - and more importantly, reliable, have the trust and protection of Villains and basically untuchable<br /> <br /> Once you fills a niche and build up your reputation business will bloom<br /> Money, favors, boons, being on the good side of the Prince or Archbishop (or hey, why not both! Be a neutral ground where Sabbat and Camarilla can drink freely without any danger<br /> Maybe even talk... ), let the social butterflies always hold in their hands your drinks, be a <i>Provider</i><br /> <br /> From there it is really depends<i> what you need </i>for payment<br /> Want money, lazy vampires would play good money for bags of blood... or delivered meal<br /> Want fame?<br /> Want boons and favors?<br /> Stockpile of weapons no question asked?<br /> Information? (Even the hardest Nosferatu would &quot;break&quot; when he face the opportunity to be in a place where he is not tolerated but<i> treated as an equal patron </i>and can drink freely and be around just like a fancy Toreador and in your Bar - your Elysium? Domain? - if you set up the rules; sure deep down he would know it is forced and fake, but turth to be told lies easly become <i>habits</i>)<br /> <br /> Scuh business could be just a little part of the backstory, could be a solo thing or a coterie working together and trust me, a tons of source of stories!<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 03-04-2026, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T20:43:45-08:00","id":1558648,"title":"","content":"In 5th edition, this is basically the Circulatory System. It's an organization of human trafficking that move people and blood from one place to another. It's primary clients are Ventrue and others with specific feeding habits, but logically it would provide merchandise to Kindred social clubs. The people &quot;on tap&quot; at a Succubus Club are likely the sort of people who aren't going to be missed if something happens to them. Still, I expect that such clubs definitely frown on vampires killing their merchandise, and those who do have to start paying higher premiums up front or quickly find themselves banned from such establishments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T22:17:13-08:00","id":1558650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1558648#post1558648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 5th edition, this is basically the Circulatory System.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they provide any guidance on fees/charges? Or is this too just hand waved by the ST?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if this can actually be implemented in an actual chronicle. <br /> <br /> Because if you make blood available for something that is merely a nominal fee or hand waved, you essentially destroy the most limiting factor on Kindred - the need to always hunt for blood. It just becomes a game about people with superpowers at that point.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly OK to make the rare instance of someone getting blood for &quot;free&quot; in order to depict a &quot;cool&quot; scene with flavor text. But I and my players are more sophisticated now, and if I introduce a place that &quot;sells&quot; blood, instead of simply accepting it for the scene and moving on, they'll want to know how to use this resource going forward. And I just can't figure out a way that properly balances things. So as much as I've seen this mentioned in other chronicles, it doesn't seem viable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T02:40:35-08:00","id":1558656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1558650#post1558650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if you make blood available for something that is merely a nominal fee or hand waved, you essentially destroy the most limiting factor on Kindred - the need to always hunt for blood. It just becomes a game about people with superpowers at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with your analysis, but that does sound like a potentially interesting setting thread. Though one that would potentially reshape the setting.<br /> <br /> A vampire society that systematically does the hunting for vampires, is potentially a more powerful and dangerous organisation. However, it's also a lot more vulnerable to disruption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T08:05:27-08:00","id":1558680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1558650#post1558650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they provide any guidance on fees/charges? Or is this too just hand waved by the ST?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To my understanding, Vampires will generally end up paying more with favors than cash. The peoples running the Circulator System have a lot of ways to make money (they can sell people to mortals as easily as vampires). So when dealing with vampires, they're more likely to ask for favors or get other things that they can't just get from mortals. So if you're constantly dropping by the Succubus Club or whatever getting blood, you'll end up owing a lot of favors. That's isn't exactly a bad thing because now you're running around doing stuff for the chronicle. Functionally you're still roleplaying how you get blood. Instead of &quot;doing a mission&quot; and getting a blood as a reward, first you get the blood and then you &quot;do a mission.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T21:45:20-08:00","id":1558696,"title":"","content":"Kindred trading favors seems more likely in regards to the Circulationry System then cash especially with the older ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T05:16:13-07:00","id":1558746,"title":"","content":"The logical fix to avoid making things TOO easy for the average vampire is to make blood cheaper to hunt than to buy - emphasise that this is a luxury (and very possibly often a return for Special Services), rather than an everyday commodity,<br /> <br /> Elders might be able to buy blood for the asking, but as ever junior Kindred have to do things the hard and nasty way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T22:02:27-07:00","id":1558783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1558656#post1558656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vampire society that systematically does the hunting for vampires, is potentially a more powerful and dangerous organisation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The scenario I am talking about it is just a local establishment that caters to Kindred and provides vitae as part of that, not a government that takes it upon itself to feed the entire vampire community. Your scenario is interesting, but different from mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1558680#post1558680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my understanding, Vampires will generally end up paying more with favors than cash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally that's what vampires need (boons) because they have trivially easy ways to get money when they want to. However, it seems that it's still not established what one would charge for, say, one blood point at such a club. It seems this gets handwaved even for the Circulatory System.<br /> <br /> Now, if this was somebody negotiating the sale to someone for their herd, I could wing that in terms of what's owed because that is not a typical transaction. But in regards to someone at a Succubus Club equivalent, you need some kind of standard pricing that makes sense for it to be 1) something a Kindred might do (possibly on a regular basis), and 2) still be more &quot;expensive&quot; than one hunting on their own to make up for the convenience versus hunting. And it doesn't seem that this has ever been worked out.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it is what I expected, but I wanted to check in case anyone had ever made that work in game from a practical perspective instead of just handwaving it to happen to showcase a &quot;cool&quot; scene.<br /> <br /> So I'll just avoid this trope in my own chronicles. Still, I'm somewhat surprised that more players haven't experienced this in their games. I have had multiple STs who have portrayed this in their games. I thought it was typical in other chronicles people have played.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T03:45:51-07:00","id":1558788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1558783#post1558783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scenario I am talking about it is just a local establishment that caters to Kindred and provides vitae as part of that, not a government that takes it upon itself to feed the entire vampire community. Your scenario is interesting, but different from mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. My point is that such a local establishment is going to become the local government quite rapidly. Like, you're making the local vampires dependant on you for their food supply, that gives the owner massive influence over local society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T21:19:27-07:00","id":1558830,"title":"","content":"If you wanted a relatively straightforward system, I'd imagine you would set it up where you can get X Blood Points with Y Resources on Z timeline, to represent vampires with sufficient wealth that they can feed somewhat regularly in that fashion.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Resources O: the Kindred can afford 1 BP per month without overextending financially.<br /> <br /> Resources OO: the Kindred can afford 1 BP per week without overextending.<br /> <br /> Resources OOO: the Kindred can afford 1 BP per day.<br /> <br /> Resources OOOO: 3 BP per day.<br /> <br /> Resources OOOOO: 10 BP per day.<br /> <br /> * the numbers are just spitballs, and would probably need to be tuned ttuthe needs of the chronicle <br /> <br /> Anyone without the sufficient level of Resources, or has hit the limit of their 'budget,' can then engage via Boons/favours, AKA plot hooks. Probably plenty of members of that kind of organization who are paid in blood themselves.<br /> <br /> As for why it doesn't feature more heavily in VtM, I'd guess it's because that kind of business is pretty risky to the Masquerade. IIRC even most typical Herd members aren't really supposed to know that they are vamp-chow. So trying to keep enough people on hand to feed a community of Kindred is creating a lot of potential witnesses who have probably seen way more than most vampires would like.<br /> <br /> I think most fictional settings that feature that sort of stuff tend to presume an ironclad Masquerade, with vampires controlling *everything.* In contrast, while VtM loves its undead puppetmasters, the drama of having to maintain the Masquerade is a big part of the story, and it might cheapen it if vampires are too known fr grossly reckless displays of their predatory nature.<br /> <br /> Not saying it doesn't/shouldn't happen. But I'd bet it's more common in Sabbat domains, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T12:45:42-07:00","id":1558839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1558788#post1558788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so. My point is that such a local establishment is going to become the local government quite rapidly. Like, you're making the local vampires dependant on you for their food supply, that gives the owner massive influence over local society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Your scenario implies that the establishment's provision of blood is superior to what the Kindred can do on their own, and that is probably not the case. I imagine that most vampires would do far better getting their own blood. Yes, if you are at the club itself, enjoying/consuming one or two blood points may be convenient, but you would be paying a premium to do so. The &quot;cost&quot; (whatever that is to be determined) should be higher than getting it yourself. And there are also lots of other disadvantages to it as well - a centralized distribution point has its own risks of disruption, security risks, delays, inconvenience (since you are not always there), quality control, etc.<br /> <br /> People can get all their alcoholic drinks at bars and eat all the time at restaurants, but there is a reason why most people don't. It's more expensive than getting it themselves, grocery stores are usually more convenient and ubiquitous, they can get exactly what they want as opposed to whatever it is that establishment serves, etc.<br /> <br /> Certainly in my scenario, such an establishment would not be superior (overall) to the Kindred getting their own blood. It's simply a convenience offered for Kindred who happen to already be there, and would be more &quot;expensive&quot; accordingly. The establishment has its own expenses and costs to cover after all that would get baked into the price, not to mention the normal effects of supply and demand. There is always likely to be far higher potential demand at such places than the establishment could safely offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-17T03:37:03-07:00","id":1558909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1558830#post1558830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted a relatively straightforward system, I'd imagine you would set it up where you can get X Blood Points with Y Resources on Z timeline, to represent vampires with sufficient wealth that they can feed somewhat regularly in that fashion.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Resources O: the Kindred can afford 1 BP per month without overextending financially.<br /> <br /> Resources OO: the Kindred can afford 1 BP per week without overextending.<br /> <br /> Resources OOO: the Kindred can afford 1 BP per day.<br /> <br /> Resources OOOO: 3 BP per day.<br /> <br /> Resources OOOOO: 10 BP per day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to much, there wasn't much of a point to invest in Herd, Fame or Domain, when the higher levels of resources allows you to get that much Blood.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T09:01:47-07:00","id":1561653,"title":"","content":"Trading boons for blood sounds like a good default but I wouldn't mind some cities trading it for cash. It's easy to limit supply, doesn't matter if you're a millionaire and a bloodbag is 100usd bloodlines style if it's 3 per person per week.<br /> <br /> Then if you want you can add in having to suck up to the traders, do favors, or stab them in the back to get your personal cap raised. Should be easy to calibrate. As long as bought blood is only readily available to a few well connected individuals it should be fine.<br /> <br /> The main limiting factor of traded blood should be it tastes awful. It's there for the desperate and the rough.<br /> <br /> Shouldn't last that long either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T01:27:12-07:00","id":1561757,"title":"","content":"<i>Giovanni Chronicles III: The Sun Has Set</i> introduces the idea of blood houses\u2014Sabbat safehouses where they can feast before raids. That might provide some inspiration? Which reminds me... I've been meaning to compile the info for the WWWiki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T06:12:29-07:00","id":1561761,"title":"","content":"I think you should just consider what real establishments with limited provisions of something special do: limit/gatekeep it.<br /> <br /> 1. Set an acceptable frequency: 1 Blood Point per Week, for example.<br /> <br /> 2. Set a business goal: is this service to ingratiate oneself with the community? To get some favors here and there? Or to exploit the desperate? That defines your base price if It's a Trivial -&gt; Minor -&gt; Major Boom.<br /> <br /> 3. Set a price increase and hard limit: start with each +1 BP increasing the severity of the Boom rather than incurring more, adjust if you want. Max, let's say 3 BP a week.<br /> <br /> 4. Set a penalty for going overboard or killing a vessel. At the very least they own a Major Boom and the vessel's replacement.<br /> <br /> 5. As an option, once a month or two there may be a party at Elysium with more blood/lower prices.<br /> <br /> Important observations:<br /> <br /> - The rules don't need to be spelled out. It's &quot;free&quot; until the customers realize it isn't.<br /> <br /> - Prices don't preclude enforcement or favoritism.<br /> <br /> - You can use the logistics as excuse to change limits and prices mid-chronicle.<br /> <br /> - No need to overthink logistics: with a limit, and possibly a limit on attending patrons, you'd need at most, if extremely realistic, 5 or 6 mortals per patron, assuming 1 BP, as 1 month is about the safe time to recover the iron levels in the marrow.<br /> <br /> - Bottled blood doesn't have to be cold. Sorcery being used to store blood fresh is a staple of the setting.<br /> <br /> - For V5 halve the amounts above. Each Hunger slaked is about 2 Blood Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T11:04:20-07:00","id":1561774,"title":"","content":"That sounds great Montparnasse and a great way to get boons of all sorts from older and more powerful Kindred and get a good degree of protection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T14:24:13-07:00","id":1562056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1561761#post1561761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should just consider what real establishments with limited provisions of something special do: limit/gatekeep it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me that sounds like a general idea of trading boons for what is essentially points of the Herd background. At least in terms of the in-character setting, mechanically it's not the same thing as you're actually getting Blood Points instead of extra dice for the Hunting roll.<br /> <br /> Negotiate with your players what a good combination of Boons to blood point frequency is, and then establish that in character. There should be a premium to that price because someone is basically subsidizing laziness.<br /> <br /> How would that actually work in the original scenario I laid out? A Kindred safe entertainment venue that supplies a certain amount of blood to its guests for refreshment? Such places would be equivalent to the Succubus Club in Chicago, the Vampire Club in San Francisco, or Club Zombie or A Taste of LA in Los Angeles. The intended purpose isn't really to replace feeding, but just as a means to add to or sustain the enjoyment of their guests. So probably limited to a single Blood Point mechanically (and maybe not even that), though some guests might imbibe one or two Blood Points at a single night. The typical &quot;wine glass&quot; of blood (probably cold and from the storage) consumed probably doesn't even qualify as a Blood Point.<br /> <br /> I guess that would probably qualify as one Trivial Boon over the course of a month. Or maybe every three months. Maybe longer if they're quite moderate in their taking. The venue keeps track of it. Said Kindred might even be given some kind of wristband to people on the list so servers know who can order such refreshments. Should the user begin to consume more blood than intended, the venue informs the Kindred that they'll need to upgrade to a minor boon for the time period. An increase to minor boon could also cover blood taken from fresher sources, or perhaps even allowed to be taken from living people (either blood bonded or dominated, and probably under supervision to make sure the Kindred does not take more than she should) provided by the venue.<br /> <br /> Under such a system, if you don't take advantage of it during that time period, probably tough luck. Though the venue owner/controller probably does his best to extend credit or be reasonable simply in order to not alienate clientele unjustly.<br /> <br /> Most Kindred probably do not bother to purchase such things, but there will be some who are peckish and want it.<br /> <br /> The venue's Kindred controller will soon end up with a wide variety of trivial boons from a huge range of Kindred. While that Kindred might just sit on it, I don't think there's much value in stockpiling such trivial boons. It's a lot to keep track of, the benefits are low, and a Kindred might not even know what to do with many of them. Instead, that Kindred will have a side business where he trades those trivial boons to people who could use them. So she's very much of a broker. Her real business is providing trivial services to other Kindred. Someone just needs access to a low level Auspex power for one night? Needs help making a mortal forget something? Use of someone's Influence or ability to do something in the mortal world that someone else's Allies or Contacts to handle? Just go to the Kindred venue owner as she's sitting on stuff.<br /> <br /> Of course, if all the venue owner is getting it out of it is more trivial boons, that's not very helpful. So instead the venue owner should be looking for a higher boon in return, like a minor boon that puts the supplicant more in depth, and negotiates some kind of long term service or clientage in exchange for the ability to call upon multiple trivial boons over time. (One part of such clientage is probably &quot;if anyone acts up in the venue, I can rely on you to help me deal with them physically if needed&quot;).<br /> <br /> All of this would be known in advance so anyone who does want to trade trivial boons for such refreshments know they'll be paying off random people. That would eliminate a lot of people from bothering to do it, but certain Kindred who are very social and like to show off their reputation in the community, might still want to do it. After all, if most Kindred can't consume vitae at all at certain venues, then those who do (even if not a full blood point) probably enjoy a little bit more status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T15:50:22-07:00","id":1562061,"title":"","content":"I like where monteparnas and Black Fox landed: treat it as a gatekept luxury, not a feeding replacement. The venue's real product isn't the vitae, it's the convenience and status, so the price should always sting a little more than just hunting would. Tjalei's point about it tasting awful is a great built-in limiter too. And I'd lean into Michael's warning as a feature, not a bug: let the proprietor accumulate quiet influence over time, which gives the ST a slow-burn plot hook rather than a broken economy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29129-daria22","name":"daria22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-22T18:33:27-07:00","id":1562067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558625-kindred-venues-that-sell-blood?p=1562056#post1562056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would that actually work in the original scenario I laid out? A Kindred safe entertainment venue that supplies a certain amount of blood to its guests for refreshment? Such places would be equivalent to the Succubus Club in Chicago, the Vampire Club in San Francisco, or Club Zombie or A Taste of LA in Los Angeles. The intended purpose isn't really to replace feeding, but just as a means to add to or sustain the enjoyment of their guests. So probably limited to a single Blood Point mechanically (and maybe not even that), though some guests might imbibe one or two Blood Points at a single night. The typical &quot;wine glass&quot; of blood (probably cold and from the storage) consumed probably doesn't even qualify as a Blood Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd simplify/generalize some things.<br /> <br /> Places like this would have distinct goals, but for venues like the Succubus Club the point is actually to subsidize the baseline amount.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: the proprietor isn't transacting mainly in boons, but in social position. Kindred come to their place to negotiate, they're a pillar of local community. The Prince may in practice owe them regular Minor or Major Boons just for the benefits in social control.<br /> <br /> Don't track trivial Boons, instead the point is the web: everyone owes them something, even if minor, and that's someone floating a little above the tangled mess of Boons. They don't need to traffic in trivial Boons, either, they build greater Boons out of those: you need something? They can get it. Not by asking a Coterie to do a quest or something, but asking a series of trivial favors from several people that chain into something greater.<br /> <br /> All combined means everyone is their friend. Most can't even keep track of their debts. Even those who avoid may feel quite deep in it, as that one time they used it was a real need, and feels more than just a Trivial Boon even if technically isn't. For many the place also works as insurance, and the clientele itself is a bonus, you go there for the vampires you find there, maybe other things, and the place is it's own thing.<br /> <br /> That's why the first Blood Point can be subsidized, and if you want Succubus Club vibes it should. The Blood is not the product, it is an investment, and the regular Boons aren't the payment, they're the grease of the system. Many places IRL work like that, btw.<br /> <br /> From a setting perspective, giving this for free won't change much: you have a slightly higher baseline for the city, but not enough to trump the value of hunting and having your own Herd. Your benefit is everyone's benefit, and partaking almost an obligation, a social ritual. And the one in the middle an unavoidable power in the city, someone you'll always deal with from a weaker position.<br /> <br /> Of course, the higher cost services and amounts add to this, and the free Blood is a good hook. And some just sell at a premium always, they're in the business for aggressive maneuvers, not slow subtlety.<br /> <br /> Don't worry too much about formalizing values. That makes sense for Neurodivergent minds, but &quot;normies&quot; get the same with cues. Leave the formal tracks out of character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}